I walk past the leather jackets.
One jacket is really beautiful.
It is soft and dark brown.
That is exactly my style.
I often wear brown clothes.
I look for size thirty-eight.
I find the beautiful jacket in my size.
I put the new leather jacket on.
Then I stand in front of the mirror.
The brown jacket fits perfectly.
It suits me fantastically.
Then I look at the price tag.
The jacket costs two hundred and fifty Euro.
That is a lot of money.
The leather jacket is wonderful, but it is much too expensive.
I do not buy the expensive jacket.
I hang it back onto the clothes rail.
